namespace pdg { /**

\fn pdg::TileLayer::getMapData(mapWidth, mapHeight, srcX, srcY)

\brief Extract a rectangular region of tile data from the layer

This function extracts a rectangular region of tile data from the TileLayer and returns it as a MemBlock containing the tile indices.

\param mapWidth The width of the region to extract in tiles. Defaults to the layer's current world width.
\param mapHeight The height of the region to extract in tiles. Defaults to the layer's current world height.
\param srcX The X coordinate of the top-left corner of the region to extract. Defaults to zero.
\param srcY The Y coordinate of the top-left corner of the region to extract. Defaults to zero.

\details
The function returns a MemBlock containing tile indices arranged in row-major order (left to right, top to bottom). Each byte in the returned data represents a tile index from the specified region.

The extracted data can be used with TileLayer::loadMapData() to copy tile data between layers or save it for later use.

\return A MemBlock containing the tile indices from the specified region

\throws RangeError If the requested width or height, including the source offset, exceeds the layer's world dimensions.
\note The returned data format is compatible with TileLayer::loadMapData(Uint8Array, int, int, int, int)

\sa TileLayer::loadMapData(Uint8Array, int, int, int, int)
\sa TileLayer::loadMapData(MemBlock, int, int, int, int)
\sa MemBlock

**/ }
